From 80307b3927b519911f1ddb492477e45030f2cccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Gonzalez <dev@gonzalezerik.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:10:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] bsps/powerpc/ibookg3: New BSP

Add a BSP for the Apple iBook G3 (PowerPC 750, NewWorld Open Firmware,
KeyLargo). It reads the machine description from the Open Firmware
device tree at boot, uses the KeyLargo ESCC channel A as a polled
console and the decrementer as the clock. The KeyLargo OpenPIC
interrupts are dispatched through the generic interrupt support with
nesting, and the OpenPIC inter-processor interrupts sent to the
processor itself serve as software interrupts. The work area is sized
from the RAM reported by Open Firmware.

It runs on QEMU's mac99 machine with -cpu 750cx.
